<title>SWITZERLAND: ATHLETICS-GEBRSELASSIE SMASHES ANOTHER RECORD.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-GEBRSELASSIE SMASHES ANOTHER RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ethiopian Haile Gebrselassie smashed his own 5,000 metres world record when he clocked 12 minutes 41.86 seconds on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Gebrselassie raced clear on the final lap to better the previous mark of 12:44.39 he had set at the same Zurich meeting in August 1995.</p>
<p>World champion Daniel Komen came second in 12:44.90 and Kenyan Paul Tergat was a distant third in 12:49.87.</p>
<p>Gebrselassie concentrated on the 10,000 metres in the recent world championships in Athens, winning the gold medal.</p>
<p>He also holds the world record for that event -- 26:31.32 set in Oslo last month.</p>
</text>
